# itel labels 26 vendor HIDL interfaces that device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr does
# not. Most are for Transsion services this tree deliberately does not ship, and
# a label for an interface nothing serves is dead weight — so only the ones with
# a shipped provider AND a measured denial are carried here.
#
# The Goodix daemon is the one that qualifies: the fingerprint HAL we ship tries
# to publish it at start and is refused. All four spellings share one type in
# stock; only IGoodixFingerprintDaemon was observed being added on build 61, and
# the siblings are carried with it because they are the same interface family
# and would fail the same way.
#
# Deliberately NOT carried, with reasons, so this is not re-litigated:
#   ITrancamserver          the provider IS shipped but never starts — its
#                           binary has no exec type, so init cannot transition
#                           into it. Labelling the interface would leave the
#                           camera finding something nothing serves. That needs
#                           a domain of its own; separate change.
#   IFpsensorHidlSvc        a probe for a fingerprint vendor this unit does not
#                           have (no /dev/fpsensor, no /dev/silead_fp).
#   INxpNfc, INxpNfcLegacy  the finds were denied only while the NFC HAL was
#                           failing to start. With /dev/pn553 labelled the HAL
#                           comes up, NFC works, and these stopped appearing —
#                           they were downstream of the real defect, not a
#                           defect themselves.
vendor.goodix.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint::IGoodixFingerprintDaemon          u:object_r:goodix_fingerprint_service:s0
vendor.goodix.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint::IGoodixFingerprintDaemonExt       u:object_r:goodix_fingerprint_service:s0
vendor.goodix.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint::IGoodixFingerprintDaemonHbd       u:object_r:goodix_fingerprint_service:s0
vendor.goodix.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint::IGoodixFingerprintDaemonFido      u:object_r:goodix_fingerprint_service:s0
